  "methodology": [
    "Create the fixture outside the timed recording/validation runs.",
    "Each measured phase runs in its own fresh process. Peak RSS is captured by /usr/bin/time.",
    "Recording streams directory entries, reads actual metadata, and commits each batch. Time includes the final WAL checkpoint.",
    "Validation streams the actual filesystem and compares every receipt against indexed database rows in batches, then checks the total count. It detects missing, unexpected and metadata-changed entries.",
    "Scan reads and consumes every stored row in reverse path order without filesystem metadata checks.",
    "Repeat the million-file phases three times with separate fresh databases. A 100,000-file control runs once.",
    "Edited, added and missing-file rejection checks passed on a separate 1,024-file smoke fixture."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "OS filesystem and inode caches were not flushed; these are warm-cache local-storage measurements, not cold-cache, NAS or HDD results.",
    "RSS covers the standalone process, including Go and SQLite, but excludes reclaimable kernel filesystem caches. The idle standalone executable measured 6,896 KiB RSS.",
    "This is metadata validation only; it does not hash file contents, execute undo, or provide an atomic snapshot against concurrent filesystem changes.",
    "The flat empty-file fixture does not measure file-content transfer buffers, deep traversal, or long-path distributions.",
    "SQLite cache_size is a cache target, not a hard whole-process memory limit."
  ],
